  "description": "This notification seeks prior approval for the installation of a roof-mounted solar photovoltaic (PV) array system with a total capacity of 320.32kWp at Ashmole Academy, Cecil Rd, London N14 5RJ.\nThe proposed array shall consist of approximately 704no solar modules, each with a nominal output of 455W. It is proposed that these be installed on the building's southeast and southwest-facing curved roof areas. Panels will be installed on a K2 pitched roof mounting kit, with the roof slope and orientation maintained. A structural assessment has been completed to ensure the roof's structural capability to support the Solar PV array, including wind and snow loading.\nThe installation shall fully comply with Building Regulations. All electrical installations will comply with all relevant standards (BSEN 7671, etc.). The system will connect to the existing electrical infrastructure with export capability via a grid-compliant connection, for which permission has been requested from the Distribution Network Operator (DNO).\nThe installation is forecasted to generate 292,990 kWh of renewable electricity in its first year of operation, contributing significantly to the site's decarbonisation and carbon emission reduction goals. The project supports local and national renewable energy goals by reducing the site's carbon footprint by approximately 52 tonnes per annum.\nThe Solar PV Panels will be mounted on the existing pitched roof. The solar installation will have a low profile and not protrude more than 200mm from the height of the proposed roofline, ensuring minimal visual impact from ground level and all surrounding viewpoints.\nMaterials have been specified to prevent glare, minimising any risk of glare for surrounding properties. The system installation will involve minimal disruption, with works expected to be completed within seven weeks. This installation will not involve significant external plant, equipment, or infrastructure beyond the roof-mounted panels and associated electrical connections.\nAll works will adhere to local planning policies, noise limits, working hours restrictions and all national construction standards. The site does not lie within any specific Planning Policy Designations, including but not limited to Green Belt, AONB, Conservation Area, Listed Building Setting, AGLV, Ecology Designation, SSSI/SAC/SPC/Other, or Scheduled Monuments. Nor does the site lie in the vicinity of any airports, airfields or any major national highways. We trust this description provides all the necessary details required.",
